# TODO - Finish source-only hardening/documentation

## Required reference workflow and files

Use `.references/` at the repository root for all retained source research.
Populate it with `python3 -B tools/references/download.py`; use `--offline`
to verify existing sources. Search ignored references explicitly with
`rg --hidden --no-ignore -g '!**/.git/**' -n 'symbol|register|error' .references/`
and enumerate files with `rg --files --hidden --no-ignore .references/`.
Whenever a behavior, API or missing implementation is unclear, search these
sources and the web for the evidence needed (prefer upstream source, published
specifications and official documentation). Record exact revisions, source
hashes, adaptation scope, destinations and licenses in the single
`.references/ledger.jsonl`. Preserve upstream notices; downloaded code is not
proof of implementation or runtime success.

Concrete files for this task (paths are relative to the repository root):

- `.references/linux/docs/process/license-rules.rst` — file-level Linux licensing rules.
- `.references/MacKernelSDK/Headers/IOKit/IOMemoryDescriptor.h` — mapping and DMA lifetime review.
- `.references/linux/net/mac80211/key.c` — key erasure/replacement review.
- `.references/nvidia-macos-driver/7412cdde81447f78da0ebb64216dc258d8beaedb/LICENSE` — PolyForm Noncommercial scope; do not treat it as GPL-compatible.
- `.references/ledger.jsonl` — scope, hash, destination and license assessments.

## Objective

After 100% production implementation and zero-failure validation, continue
edge-case hardening indefinitely while the owner tests the notebook and
shares logs in this conversation. This work is parallel to authorized testing;
its ongoing status must never block every hardware test indefinitely.

Reason through bounds, overflow, lifetime, crypto erasure, regulatory safety,
deadlocks, interrupt races, rollback, licensing and documentation. Keep
README/AGENTS/TODO accurate. Use tools/validate.py for installed Clang, Ruff
and BasedPyright checks plus necessary offline host tests; no Jig, new
frameworks, kext compilation, CI or hardware diagnostics.

